---
title: Display Defaults
---

Beyond feature flags, `app-config.json` also controls the default visual settings of the video room — the starting resolution and room layout.

## Video Resolution

`videoSettings.defaultResolution` sets the outgoing video resolution when a participant joins.

| Value | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `1920x1080` | Full HD |
| `1280x960` | HD (4:3) |
| `1280x720` | HD 720p **(default)** |
| `640x480` | SD (4:3) |
| `640x360` | SD 360p |
| `320x240` | Low (4:3) |
| `320x180` | Low 180p |

```json
{
  "videoSettings": {
    "defaultResolution": "1280x720"
  }
}
```

## Room Layout

`meetingRoomSettings.defaultLayoutMode` controls which layout is shown when a participant first enters the room.

| Value | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `activeSpeaker` | Highlights the current speaker **(default)** |
| `grid` | Shows all participants in an equal grid |

```json
{
  "meetingRoomSettings": {
    "defaultLayoutMode": "activeSpeaker"
  }
}
```

{% aside type="caution" %}
Changing `meetingRoomSettings.defaultLayoutMode` requires the participant to **rejoin the room** to take effect — a running session does not update dynamically.
{% /aside %}

## Custom Video Bitrate Range

These settings control the minimum and maximum selectable bitrate in the **Advanced Settings** dialog.

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `MIN_CUSTOM_VIDEO_BITRATE_BPS` | `5000` | Minimum selectable bitrate in bps |
| `MAX_CUSTOM_VIDEO_BITRATE_BPS` | `10000000` | Maximum selectable bitrate in bps |

## Supported Frame Rates

`SUPPORTED_FRAME_RATES` defines the frame rate options shown in the Advanced Settings video tab. Values are positive integers separated by `|`.

`PUBLISHER_MAX_RESOLUTION` (`1920x1080`), `NOTIFICATION_DURATION_MS` (`4000`), the bitrate values above, and `SUPPORTED_FRAME_RATES` (`30|15|7|1`) are currently fixed defaults and cannot be overridden without a code change.

{% aside type="tip" %}
Lowering `videoSettings.defaultResolution` can significantly reduce bandwidth usage — useful when you know participants may be on slower connections.
{% /aside %}

You have configured the display defaults. In the next step, you will apply all your changes and verify them.
